---
// Case study diagram (/des-sys-audit): what happens after the skill's report. Every recommendation
// goes through a person: verify it, fix Figma, test the code in Cursor, compare the two, and shim
// where rendering differences leave them visibly off. The last two steps repeat until they match.

const steps = [
  { title: 'Verify', body: 'Check each recommendation and why it was flagged' },
  { title: 'Fix Figma', body: 'Make the design changes that are clearly needed' },
  { title: 'Test in code', body: 'Apply the code changes in Cursor and preview them' },
  { title: 'Compare', body: 'Put design and code side by side to catch visual drift' },
  { title: 'Shim', body: 'Where text sits differently, add a small offset in design or code' },
];
---

<figure class="audit-loop">
  <ol class="audit-loop-steps">
    {
      steps.map((step, i) => (
        <li class:list={['audit-step', i >= 3 && 'is-looped']}>
          <span class="audit-step-number">{i + 1}</span>
          <strong>{step.title}</strong>
          <span class="audit-step-body">{step.body}</span>
        </li>
      ))
    }
  </ol>
  <div class="audit-loop-repeat">
    <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
      <path d="M4 12a8 8 0 0 1 14-5.3M20 4v4h-4M20 12a8 8 0 0 1-14 5.3M4 20v-4h4"></path>
    </svg>
    <span>Steps 4 and 5 repeat until design and code match</span>
  </div>
  <figcaption>Every step after the report is a judgment call, which is where most of the time went.</figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  .audit-loop {
    margin: var(--space-8) 0 0;
  }

  /* Specific enough to beat the case study layout's ol styles */
  .audit-loop ol.audit-loop-steps {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-3);
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
  }

  @media (min-width: 640px) {
    .audit-loop ol.audit-loop-steps {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(5, minmax(0, 1fr));
    }
  }

  /* The stat card panel, reused as a step */
  .audit-step {
    display: grid;
    align-content: start;
    gap: var(--space-1);
    padding: var(--space-4);
    background: var(--color-surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-base);
  }

  /* The repeating steps: dashed, to tie them to the loop note below */
  .audit-step.is-looped {
    border-style: dashed;
    border-color: var(--color-border-strong);
  }

  .audit-step-number {
    display: inline-grid;
    place-items: center;
    width: var(--space-6);
    height: var(--space-6);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
    border-radius: var(--radius-base);
    background: var(--color-ink);
    color: var(--color-canvas);
    font: var(--type-count);
  }

  .audit-step strong {
    font: var(--type-label);
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-body);
    color: var(--color-ink);
  }

  .audit-step .audit-step-body {
    font: var(--type-compact);
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-body);
    color: var(--color-muted);
  }

  .audit-loop-repeat {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--space-2);
    margin-top: var(--space-3);
    padding: var(--space-3) var(--space-4);
    border: 1px dashed var(--color-border-strong);
    border-radius: var(--radius-base);
    font: var(--type-compact);
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-body);
    color: var(--color-muted);
  }

  /* On wide screens the note sits under steps 4 and 5 only */
  @media (min-width: 640px) {
    .audit-loop-repeat {
      margin-left: calc(60% + var(--space-3) * 0.6);
    }
  }

  .audit-loop-repeat svg {
    flex: none;
    width: var(--space-4);
    height: var(--space-4);
    fill: none;
    stroke: currentColor;
    stroke-width: 1.5;
    stroke-linecap: round;
    stroke-linejoin: round;
  }

  .audit-loop figcaption {
    margin-top: var(--space-2);
    font: var(--type-body);
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-body);
    color: var(--color-muted);
  }
</style>
